id: pm-j82fd3
title: "Outcome milestone: agent-legible command grammar — one-screen surface, zero feature loss, alias-preserved"
description: "Outcome milestone for an agent-legible command grammar: a one-screen noun-verb surface with complete contracts, lossless aliases, and measured token savings."
type: Milestone
status: open
priority: 1
tags[6]: agent-ux,grammar,"horizon:near",milestone,outcome,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-07-24T23:42:39.540Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-28T13:20:32.643Z"
deadline: "2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 4800
acceptance_criteria: Top-level command count meets the pm-pbyu ADR target with zero capability removed; Every pre-consolidation spelling resolves via the alias shim with a one-line migration hint; Golden agent-transcript replay shows a measured tokens-per-completed-task reduction versus the pre-consolidation baseline; Tiered help renders the full core surface in one screen; pm help --all remains complete
goal: agent-legible-surface
objective: A coding agent operates every pm capability from one screen of help without out-of-band context
value: "Cuts the dominant agent onboarding cost: today's ~70 top-level commands force out-of-band documentation reads before the first useful call."
impact: Every agent invocation in every downstream workspace gets cheaper; the grammar freeze in the GA contract depends on this landing first.
outcome: "Top-level noun count at or below the ADR target, every retired spelling still functional as a hidden alias, and a measured drop in tokens-per-completed-task."
why_now: "The surface is still growing (graph, plan, merge, history-* families all landed post-v0.1). Consolidating later means freezing more aliases forever."
parent: pm-doxj
risk: medium
confidence: high
expected_result: "The command surface fits one screen, no capability was removed, every old spelling resolves through an alias with a migration hint, and tokens per completed task measurably fell."
